  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "R8 and R18 provide a close refractory-alloy analogue: adding Cr to a WVTaTi BCC system produces a network-distributed Cr2Ta Laves phase and increases hardness through combined solid-solution and Laves-precipitation strengthening. The other records establish that minor alloying can enhance both strength and plasticity in related BCC refractory HEAs, that second phases impede dislocations, and that phase morphology can affect mechanical performance. Although none explicitly demonstrates ductility improvement through crack deflection by a reticulated Laves network, an expert could plausibly transfer the Cr-addition/network-Laves strategy to HfMoTaTiZr and propose the reported dual mechanism."
